Upstream: https://github.com/wfeldt/libx86emu
Revision: ce81129c57fdfbf690bebc210a8db97d926cc5e7
Imported: 2026-10-27

LICENSE and LICENSE_INFO retain upstream licensing information. The
upstream demo/ program and .github/ workflows are not included; the
upstream Makefile and README.md still mention them.

Amiga integration lives in src/x86emu and src/runtime. Changes to this
directory are separate commits, so `git log -- third_party/libx86emu`
lists them:

- bounded 68020 execution with an external clock and no host I/O
  (X86EMU_EXTERNAL_CLOCK, X86EMU_NO_HOST_IO)
- optional instruction text generation (X86EMU_NO_DISASSEMBLY)
- direct instruction fetch and less dispatch work (X86EMU_DIRECT_FETCH,
  X86EMU_NO_TRACE_FORMATTING)
- bounded REP MOVS/STOS and REP SCAS callbacks (X86EMU_BULK_STRINGS)
- an AAM divide error returns after raising the fault
- cached opcode decoding for the block translator's semantic fallback

The test/ directory holds the upstream regression fixtures, which
tools/check_blockjit.py runs against both CPU backends. The top-level
build pins this source; it does not download dependencies.
